From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Mason <mason@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:39:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mm/huge_memory: fix truncate racing with PMD zapping

zap_huge_pmd_folio() removes the rmap before calling folio_mark_dirty().
If this was the last mapping, truncation can skip unmapping the folio
and proceed without waiting for the PMD lock, racing with dirtying.

ifs_set_range_dirty() can oops if MADV_DONTNEED races with
ftruncate() on XFS, when we get the folio set dirty after it was found
to not be mapped anymore.

Move folio_mark_dirty() and folio_mark_accessed() before rmap removal,
matching the PTE zap path. This keeps the folio mapped while updating
its state, so truncation must wait for the page table lock.

Fix generated by an LLM and sent by Chris Mason in private.

Fixes: fe6cf984939d ("mm/huge_memory: transfer the pmd dirty bit to the folio on zap")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Chris Mason <mason@kernel.org>
[ david: simplify comment and description ]
Reviewed-by: Gregory Price (Meta) <gourry@gourry.net>
Tested-by: Muhammad Usama Anjum <usama.anjum@arm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261031-fixes_core-v3-13-d6437171ecc3@kernel.org
Reviewed-by: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Baolin Wang <baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com>
Signed-off-by: David Hildenbrand (Arm) <david@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit e6a07d29b0a60f3a4cfe77fe34eeb4b3fb38d6c4)
[TL: backport to zap_huge_pmd(), which has no zap_huge_pmd_folio() split
 out here: drop the early rmap removal of present PMDs and remove it after
 the dirty and young transfer instead, device private folios keep their
 own removal]
Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 mm/huge_memory.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/huge_memory.c b/mm/huge_memory.c
index efeec3fb8711d1c50b74f61fbdc990e310e7e315..ac5802340a0eac4eda367e0f9c9de1b1a72dc7f4 100644
--- a/mm/huge_memory.c
+++ b/mm/huge_memory.c
@@ -2435,8 +2435,6 @@ int zap_huge_pmd(struct mmu_gather *tlb, struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 			struct page *page = pmd_page(orig_pmd);
 
 			folio = page_folio(page);
-			folio_remove_rmap_pmd(folio, page, vma);
-			WARN_ON_ONCE(folio_mapcount(folio) < 0);
 			VM_BUG_ON_PAGE(!PageHead(page), page);
 		} else if (pmd_is_valid_softleaf(orig_pmd)) {
 			const softleaf_t entry = softleaf_from_pmd(orig_pmd);
@@ -2468,6 +2466,15 @@ int zap_huge_pmd(struct mmu_gather *tlb, struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 				folio_mark_accessed(folio);
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Present folios are rmappable. Remove the rmap after
+		 * transferring young+dirty to the folio.
+		 */
+		if (flush_needed) {
+			folio_remove_rmap_pmd(folio, &folio->page, vma);
+			WARN_ON_ONCE(folio_mapcount(folio) < 0);
+		}
+
 		if (folio_is_device_private(folio)) {
 			folio_remove_rmap_pmd(folio, &folio->page, vma);
 			WARN_ON_ONCE(folio_mapcount(folio) < 0);
